@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Cataract Surgery";
    Layout = "_PublicLayout";
}

<style>
    .tx-wrap {
        max-width: 1000px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 40px 24px 80px;
    }

    .tx-crumb {
        font-size: 13px;
        color: #6B7280;
        margin-bottom: 16px;
    }

        .tx-crumb a {
            color: #2B6CB0;
            text-decoration: none;
        }

    .tx-title {
        font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 30px;
        color: #0B1C30;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
        line-height: 1.3;
    }

    .tx-meta {
        display: flex;
        gap: 14px;
        font-size: 13px;
        color: #6B7280;
        margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

        .tx-meta .cat {
            color: #2B6CB0;
            font-weight: 700;
        }

    .tx-hero-img {
        width: 100%;
        height: 340px;
        object-fit: cover;
        border-radius: 14px;
        margin-bottom: 32px;
        background: #eee;
    }

    .tx-main {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;
        gap: 36px;
        align-items: start;
    }

    .tx-body p {
        font-size: 15px;
        color: #374151;
        line-height: 1.85;
        margin-bottom: 18px;
    }

    .tx-body h2 {
        font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 19px;
        color: #0B1C30;
        margin: 28px 0 12px;
    }

        .tx-body h2:first-child {
            margin-top: 0;
        }

    .tx-body ul {
        margin: 0 0 18px;
        padding-left: 20px;
    }

    .tx-body li {
        font-size: 15px;
        color: #374151;
        line-height: 1.8;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
    }

    .tx-side-box {
        background: #E9F2FF;
        border-radius: 14px;
        padding: 22px;
    }

        .tx-side-box h4 {
            font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
            font-size: 15px;
            color: #0B1C30;
            margin-bottom: 14px;
        }

        .tx-side-box ul {
            list-style: none;
            padding: 0;
            margin: 0;
        }

        .tx-side-box li {
            font-size: 13px;
            color: #374151;
            line-height: 1.6;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            padding-left: 20px;
            position: relative;
        }

            .tx-side-box li::before {
                content: "✓";
                color: #2B6CB0;
                font-weight: 700;
                position: absolute;
                left: 0;
            }

    .tx-cta {
        margin-top: 50px;
        background: #0B1C30;
        border-radius: 16px;
        padding: 40px;
        text-align: center;
        color: #fff;
    }

        .tx-cta h3 {
            font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
            font-weight: 700;
            font-size: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        .tx-cta p {
            font-size: 13px;
            opacity: 0.85;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .tx-cta a {
            display: inline-block;
            background: #2B6CB0;
            color: #fff;
            padding: 12px 26px;
            border-radius: 9999px;
            font-weight: 700;
            font-size: 13px;
            text-decoration: none;
        }

    @@media (max-width: 800px) {
        .tx-main {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }
    }
</style>

<div class="tx-wrap">
    <div class="tx-crumb"><a href="/Blog">Treatments</a> / Cataract Surgery</div>
    <h1 class="tx-title">Cataract Surgery: Advanced Care for Clearer Vision</h1>
    <div class="tx-meta">
        <span class="cat">Eye Surgery</span>
        <span>@DateTime.Now.ToString("MMM d, yyyy")</span>
    </div>

    <img class="tx-hero-img" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551076805-e1869033e561" alt="Cataract Surgery" />

    <div class="tx-main">
        <div class="tx-body">
            <p>
                In a healthy eye, the natural lens is clear and transparent, allowing light to pass through
                and focus properly on the retina. A cataract develops when this lens becomes cloudy or
                opaque, scattering light instead of letting it pass through cleanly. This results in
                blurred vision, faded colors, and increased sensitivity to glare, particularly at night.
            </p>
            <p>
                Cataracts typically develop slowly with age, though they can also result from injury,
                certain medications, or underlying health conditions like diabetes. Left untreated,
                cataracts can significantly impact daily activities such as reading, driving, and
                recognizing faces.
            </p>

            <h2>Our Approach: Phacoemulsification</h2>
            <p>
                At Urmi Eye Hospital, we use phacoemulsification, the gold standard in modern cataract
                surgery. This minimally invasive technique uses high-frequency ultrasound waves to gently
                break up the cloudy lens into tiny fragments, which are then removed through a very small
                incision. A clear, artificial intraocular lens (IOL) is then implanted to restore sharp
                vision.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Typically completed in 15–20 minutes per eye</li>
                <li>Performed under local anesthesia with minimal discomfort</li>
                <li>No stitches required in most cases due to the small incision size</li>
                <li>Most patients notice improved vision within 24–48 hours</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Choosing the Right Lens</h2>
            <p>
                We offer a range of intraocular lens options tailored to your lifestyle and visual needs,
                including standard monofocal lenses, premium multifocal lenses for reduced dependency on
                glasses, and toric lenses for patients with astigmatism.
            </p>

            <h2>Recovery &amp; Aftercare</h2>
            <p>
                Recovery is typically quick, with most patients resuming normal activities within a few
                days. We provide clear post-operative instructions, prescribed eye drops, and follow-up
                visits to ensure the best possible outcome.
            </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="tx-side-box">
            <h4>Key Takeaways</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Phacoemulsification is the gold-standard technique</li>
                <li>Procedure takes just 15–20 minutes per eye</li>
                <li>Multiple lens options available for your lifestyle</li>
                <li>Most patients recover within 24–48 hours</li>
            </ul>
        </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="tx-cta">
        <h3>Ready to Experience Clearer Vision?</h3>
        <p>Schedule a comprehensive consultation with our specialists today.</p>
        <a href="/Appointment/Book">Book an Appointment &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>